    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn infinite radicals and telescoping root patterns with a small example.\n\nWe will build the method one step at a time and check each answer.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A repeating radical contains a copy of itself.\n\nLet x = √(6+√(6+√(6+...))).\nThe tail after the first 6 is again x.\nSo x=√(6+x).\nSquare: x²=6+x, or x²−x−6=0.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "input": {
        "type": "CHOICE",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "label": "x=2+x"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "label": "x²=2x"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "label": "x=2²+x"
          },
          {
            "id": "d",
            "label": "x² = 2 + x"
          }
        ]
      },
      "content": {
        "text": "If x=√(2+√(2+√(2+...))), which equation is correct?",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "field": "isCorrect",
            "value": true,
            "operator": "EQUALS"
